<title>SWEDEN: SSAB 9-MO FALLS 44 PCT.</title>
<headline>SSAB 9-MO FALLS 44 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish steelmaker SSAB reports</p>
<p>for the nine months to September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		 1,603  vs   2,859</p>
<p> Operating income			13,032  vs  14,081</p>
<p> Operating costs			 11,187  vs  10,960</p>
<p> Depreciation				 548  vs     503</p>
<p> Operating profit after deprec	1,297  vs   2,618</p>
<p> Associate interests			 54  vs	73</p>
<p> Net financial items	     CREDIT 252  vs     168</p>
<p> Minority interests			  34  vs	59</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			   1,569  vs   2,800</p>
<p> Tax charge				   432  vs     777</p>
<p> EPS (crowns)				8.90  vs   15.80</p>
<p> Net profit				 1,137  vs   2,023</p>
<p>Ex-dividend day</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuter poll found analysts expected SSAB to post a nine month profit after financial items of 1.66 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
